            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0456" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 343/50.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the German
                    Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 71.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note No. 1034 of the 7th instant bringing to my notice the matter of the
                    transportation from Tangier to New York of Paul O. Stensland on board the
                    steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Prim Adalbert</hi> of the Hamburg-Amerika
                    Line, and to say in response that the representations which you make in this
                    connection with regard to alleged irregularity on the part of the American
                    consul general at Tangier will receive consideration.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
